r:transparent" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/images/courses/coding-patterns=
/intervals/identify-all-interval-overlaps/image-09-02-2-GSFUUA7K.svg?dpl=3D=
dpl_CEjisbLnWxFQGUTRjiHGoKY1oV5c"></div></figure>
<p>Therefore, when two intervals overlap, their overlap is defined by the r=
ange <strong>[<code>B.start</code>, <code>min(A.end, B.end)</code>]</strong=
>. Remember that in all these cases, interval A always starts first.</p>
<p><strong>Identifying all overlaps</strong><br>
<!-- -->Now, let=E2=80=99s return to the two arrays of intervals. Consider =
this example:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:left"><im=
g alt=3D"Image represents a visualization of two sets of intervals, labeled=
